Z||000028||88CoupeV6||10-26-2001||08:59 PM||||OK, Here is how I did the center caps. <P>Parts needed.<BR>1. stock fiero center caps<BR>2. Rodney's center cap stickers.<BR>3. the rings I have. (sprnt96, I have 4 more I can send you. Just e-mail me your add. and I will send them out.<BR>4. JB Weld or other epoxy glue.<BR>5. electrical tape.<P>You take the center caps with Rodney's stickers and cover the clip part with the JB weld. Push the cap into the end of the ring all the way. Let that dry. Then wrap the ring with electrical tape until it pushes into the center of the wheel tightly.<P>Done  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Here is the unit from the back before the tape.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/imex3.jpg"> ||||reg||7
